msgid ""
"About **FAULT_FLAG_ALLOW_RETRY** and **FAULT_FLAG_TRIED**: we can specify "
"whether we would allow page faults to retry by specifying these two fault "
"flags correctly.  Currently there can be three legal combinations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:103: ../include/linux/mm_types.h:1793
msgid "ALLOW_RETRY and !TRIED:  this means the page fault allows retry, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:103: ../include/linux/mm_types.h:1794
msgid "this is the first try"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:103: ../include/linux/mm_types.h:1796
msgid "ALLOW_RETRY and TRIED:   this means the page fault allows retry, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:103: ../include/linux/mm_types.h:1797
msgid "we've already tried at least once"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:103: ../include/linux/mm_types.h:1799
msgid "!ALLOW_RETRY and !TRIED: this means the page fault does not allow retry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:103: ../include/linux/mm_types.h:1801
msgid ""
"The unlisted combination (!ALLOW_RETRY && TRIED) is illegal and should never "
"be used.  Note that page faults can be allowed to retry for multiple times, "
"in which case we'll have an initial fault with flags (a) then later on "
"continuous faults with flags (b).  We should always try to detect pending "
"signals before a retry to make sure the continuous page faults can still be "
"interrupted if necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/mm-api:103: ../include/linux/mm_types.h:1808
msgid ""
"The combination FAULT_FLAG_WRITE|FAULT_FLAG_UNSHARE is illegal. "
"FAULT_FLAG_UNSHARE is ignored and treated like an ordinary read fault when "
"applied to mappings that are not COW mappings."
msgstr ""

